<title>ETHIOPIA: Britain donates food to south Ethiopia.</title>
<headline>Britain donates food to south Ethiopia.</headline>
<dateline>ADDIS ABABA 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain said on Tuesday it would donate 3,000 tonnes of maize and 100 tonnes of high-protein biscuits worth nearly $1 million to help combat food shortages in Ethiopia's southern region.</p>
<p>The British embassy in Addis Ababa said the food would be distributed in Wolaita region.</p>
<p>The donation was in response to an appeal by Ethiopia's Disaster Prevention and Preparedness Commission for assistance following late seasonal rains, the embassy said.</p>
</text>
